Changelog: 13-10-2026 11:45:43

Withdrawn releases (owner's decisions, 13-10-2026): apps.toml takes withdrawn = "<reason>" in an app's entry (not for
the required app nor checkout-only apps; manifest.py). A withdrawn app's tile shows App not available in red, with the
reason; it cannot be installed or opened and shows no update. At start the portal removes a withdrawn app that is
installed, after saying why, with the app's own uninstaller in a terminal, one app after another; one that could not
be removed keeps its Uninstall button and is tried again at the next start. The portal update button names the apps a
newer portal withdraws ("withdraws ..."), with the reason in its tooltip. Older portals ignore the field. Tests: the
field and its rules, the tile, the removal at start, a removal that fails, the update comparison.

