Changelog: 11-10-2026 22:59:50

Release 0.9.10. Pins hdmi-cec-v0.1.2. optional desktop icons, hdmi-cec app update

Changelog: 11-10-2026 22:51:53

App icons on the Desktop: a switch at the top of the portal (desktop_icons.py). The portal's own icon is enough to
reach every app, so the apps' icons on the Desktop are the user's choice: on, the portal copies every installed app's
menu entry to the Desktop (executable, trusted for GNOME, as the installers do); off, it removes the Desktop copies of
the suite's menu entries, at start, after each install (the installers still write one) and when switched off. Only
files named like a suite menu entry (bc250-*.desktop in ~/.local/share/applications) are touched, never the portal's
own icon. The first start asks whether to keep the app icons when there are some; without any, the switch starts off
without asking. The app menu entries always stay. The app installers are unchanged.

